export anchor StatusMatrixStyle:
    number: 211
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Status matrix
    idea: A planning grid of projects against weeks, where each row shows this week's status as a shaped marker, hatched weeks running to a due flag, and summary rows below, read like a spreadsheet.
    base: light
    palette:
        page: #f4f5f7, the page, column heads and table footers
        paper: #ffffff, the header, panels and the matrix body
        ink: #101828, text, figures and the frozen column rule
        sub: #475467, week labels, team names and times
        grid: #d0d5dd, cell borders and panel edges, never text
        band: #e9ecf1, the tab band and initials
        blue: #175cd3, the primary button, the active tab, the this week outline, focus and the darkest heat cell
        nowTint: #eaf1fd, the this week column, the lightest heat cell and a focused row
        planBlue: #b8cdef, hatched weeks before the due date, never text
        heatMid: #b2ccf5, heat cells of 5 to 9
        heatHigh: #6f9ae8, heat cells of 10 to 13 with ink figures
        green: #067647, the On track circle and word
        rust: #8f4a00, the At risk diamond and word
        red: #b42318, the Behind crossed square and the overdue line
    type:
        Two stacks. Labels and figures use ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo,
        Consolas, Liberation Mono. Text uses Segoe UI, system-ui, Roboto,
        Helvetica Neue, Arial. Heat figures are 18px mono bold, the
        greeting 16px sans bold, project names 13px sans semibold, body
        13px, panel labels 12px mono bold caps and week heads 11px mono.
    layout:
        A two tier header. The first tier is white with a six dot brand
        mark and Brightwork in mono, a wide centred search with a slash
        key hint, a blue New project button, a square bell with a count
        and Mara Okafor. The second tier is a grey tab band with the six
        nav tabs, the current one white with a blue underline. Below, one
        white strip holds Hello, Mara, the date in mono, a crossed red
        square with 4 tasks are overdue and four outlined chips on the
        right for the summary figures. The main panel is the matrix, a
        table with a frozen project column carrying name, team, tasks and
        percent, then thirteen week columns from 18 Oct to 10 Jan. The
        18 Oct column is last week with dots. The 25 Oct column is this
        week, tinted and outlined in blue, holding each project's status
        marker and word. Following weeks are hatched blue up to a pennant
        flag cell reading the due date. A footer gives projects due per
        week and tasks completed, 59 and 73. Below, two panels side by
        side hold a calendar heat grid of the fourteen days with the count
        printed in every cell and weekly totals at the row starts, and an
        activity log table of time, person and action. The matrix scrolls
        sideways inside its panel on small screens, the search drops to its
        own row and the log rows stack.
    spacing: A 4px unit. Cells are 44px tall, panel padding 10 to 14px, 16px between panels.
    density: High. Thirteen week columns by six projects in one grid, with summary rows in the footer.
    corners: 4px on panels, buttons, fields and heat cells. Markers are sharp except the circle.
    borders: 1px cool grey lines on every cell. A 2px ink rule freezes the project column and a 2px blue outline marks this week.
    shadows: None.
    icons:
        1.8px line icons at 16px. Status markers are a filled circle for
        On track, a filled diamond for At risk and a square with a white
        cross for Behind. A pennant flag marks the due week.
    focus: A 2px blue outline offset 1px. A focused row gets the now tint.
    tone: Terse and operational, such as This wk, Projects due and Activity log.
